  "documents": [
    {
      "body": "## Staffing memo (filed copy)\n\nInterim arrangement during the ground-floor works: handovers take place in the first-floor meeting room. Uniforms can still be collected from the basement store.",
      "document_id": "doc-expired-memo",
      "effective_from": "2026-05-03",
      "effective_until": "2026-08-01",
      "source": "expired_memo",
      "title": "Old staffing memo"
    },
    {
      "body": "## Working time – what every rota must follow\n\n- Weekly hours: no more than 48 hours in any Monday–Sunday week, unless the person has signed the 48-hour opt-out.\n- Daily rest: at least 11 hours off between the end of one shift and the start of the next.\n- Weekly rest: 24 hours off in a row in every 7 days, or 48 hours in every 14 days.\n- Breaks: every shift over six hours has at least 20 minutes' break (already built into our shifts).\n- Night workers: no more than 8 hours' work on average per 24 hours.\n- Staff records are binding: nobody works on a fixed day off, outside a nights-only contract or during a recorded absence (sick calls included).\n- Each staff record shows the maximum number of nights per month for that person.\n- Nights in a row, the nurse minimum per shift, working days in a row, late-to-early and part-time margins: see the current house rules and the signed works agreement.\n\n## Shift times and breaks\n\n| Shift | Start | End | Break |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Early | 06:00 | 14:00 | 30 minutes |\n| Late | 14:00 | 22:00 | 30 minutes |\n| Night | 22:00 | 06:00 | 30 minutes |\n\n### Which rule applies?\nIf two written sources disagree, the order is: law, then the signed works agreement, then the current house rules, then memos. An expired memo does not apply. If two valid memos disagree, the newer one applies.",
      "document_id": "doc-handbook",
      "effective_from": "2025-06-06",
      "effective_until": null,
      "source": "staff_handbook",
      "title": "Staff handbook (extract): working time"
    },
    {
      "body": "## House rules for the rota\n\n- No more than 4 night shifts in a row.\n- At least 1 registered nurse on every shift on every unit.\n- No more than 5 working days in a row.\n- No early shift the morning after a late shift.\n- Part-time staff may work at most 10% above their contract hours in a Monday–Sunday week.\n\nWhere the signed agreement or the law says otherwise, that applies (order of sources: see the staff handbook).",
      "document_id": "doc-house-rules",
      "effective_from": "2025-06-23",
      "effective_until": null,
      "source": "house_rules",
      "title": "House rules for the rota (current copy)"
    },
    {
      "body": "## Forwarded email\n\nFrom: Operations manager\nTo: Home manager\nSubject: Cover over the next few weeks\n\nHi all, staffing is tight across the region at the moment. Please keep the shifts covered as best you can.",
      "document_id": "doc-manager-email",
      "effective_from": "2026-08-21",
      "effective_until": null,
      "source": "manager_email",
      "title": "Email from the operations manager (forwarded)"
    },
    {
      "body": "## Unit notes\n\n- Cedar Unit: use the qualifications shown in the rota demand; a team leader does not replace a registered nurse.",
      "document_id": "doc-ward-notes",
      "effective_from": "2026-04-10",
      "effective_until": null,
      "source": "ward_notes",
      "title": "Unit notes"
    },
    {
      "body": "## Agreement with staff representatives on rota planning (signed)\n\nBetween the provider and the elected staff representatives. Where it sets a more specific limit than the house rules, the agreement applies; stricter legal rules still apply.\n\nFor nights in a row, the current house rules apply. Enter approved swaps before the next publication.",
      "document_id": "doc-works-agreement",
      "effective_from": "2025-03-19",
      "effective_until": null,
      "source": "works_agreement",
      "title": "Staff representatives agreement (rota planning)"
    }
  ],
